Chapter: IdentityNoCap

 A child that drops its own identity bit is refused by the kernel.
 The parent declares Identity, so the grant exists and is inherited;
 the child restricts it away (Capability) and the following
 identity-set returns -1.

Section: Body
  record-result : Integer -> Integer
  record-result (set-result) = poke-byte 28000 0 (if set-result == (0 - 1) then 1 else 0)

  set-after-restrict : Integer -> [Identity] Integer
  set-after-restrict (r) = record-result (identity-set 0 999)

  child-body : Integer -> [Capability, Identity] Integer
  child-body (x) = set-after-restrict (process-restrict-cap (process-get-pid) 15)

  verdict : Integer -> Text
  verdict (child) =
    let wt = process-wait child
    in if peek-byte 28000 0 == 1 then "PASS: identity-set denied without cap-identity"
    else "FAIL: identity-set succeeded without cap"

  opening : [Console, Concurrent, Capability, Identity] Nothing = act
    child <- process-spawn (\x -> child-body x)
    print-line-uni (verdict child)
  end
